{"_id":"wmMark0000000095","name":"Precision Joinery — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-precision-joinery"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000095","name":"Precision Joinery","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Precision Joinery</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to checks to Repair, maintain or operate its crafted mechanism.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000096","name":"Reinforced Limb — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-reinforced-limb"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000096","name":"Reinforced Limb","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Limb</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>Bow/crossbow/wooden weapon gains +1 damage per damage die against objects and structures.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000097","name":"Modular Frame — Carpentry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-universal-modular-frame"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000097","name":"Modular Frame","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Modular Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Universal</p><p>One approved wooden component can be swapped during daily preparations without rebuilding the entire item.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000098","name":"True Fletching — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-true-fletching"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000098","name":"True Fletching","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>True Fletching</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ignore the first range-related environmental penalty from ordinary wind; ammunition can carry the artisan&#39;s identifying fletch.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000099","name":"Specialist Ammo Chamber — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-specialist-ammo-chamber"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000099","name":"Specialist Ammo Chamber","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Specialist Ammo Chamber</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Weapon can use one additional approved specialist ammunition family without modification.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000100","name":"Longshot Construction — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-longshot-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000100","name":"Longshot Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Longshot Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Increase range increment by 50%; first range increment beyond normal maximum does not impose an additional penalty.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000101","name":"Rapid Mechanism — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-rapid-mechanism"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000101","name":"Rapid Mechanism","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Mechanism</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Once per round reduce one reload action by 1 action, minimum 0; if already reload 0, instead gain +1 Artisan bonus to first Strike after reloading.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000102","name":"Perfected Tension — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-perfected-tension"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000102","name":"Perfected Tension","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Perfected Tension</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +1 attack beyond Core progression. Does not stack with another Over-Potency effect.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000103","name":"Warbow Overdraw — Carpentry — Warbowyer","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-1-warbow-overdraw"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000103","name":"Warbow Overdraw","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Warbow Overdraw</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warbowyer</p><p>Ranged weapon gains +1 additional base weapon damage die beyond Core progression; on a natural 1, wielder becomes off-guard until start of next turn from the violent recoil/tension.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4; Core-tier Anchor required</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000104","name":"Builder's Mark — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-builders-mark"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000104","name":"Builder's Mark","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Builder&#39;s Mark</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify structural weaknesses or repair methods in wooden construction.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000105","name":"Reinforced Frame — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-reinforced-frame"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000105","name":"Reinforced Frame","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Reinforced Frame</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Structure or wooden vehicle gains +20% HP and +2 Hardness.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000106","name":"Rapid Assembly — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-rapid-assembly"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000106","name":"Rapid Assembly","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Rapid Assembly</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Reduce qualifying construction or field-fortification time by 30%.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000107","name":"Modular Construction — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-modular-construction"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000107","name":"Modular Construction","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Modular Construction</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Structure can be dismantled/reconfigured while recovering 80% of ordinary materials; temporary field works can be deployed in half normal time.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000108","name":"Grand Design — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-grand-design"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000108","name":"Grand Design","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Design</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Kingdom project using this design reduces one recurring Lumber/repair cost by 25% and gains +2 Artisan bonus to its primary construction check.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000109","name":"Citadel Framework — Carpentry — Masterwright","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-2-citadel-framework"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000109","name":"Citadel Framework","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Citadel Framework</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Masterwright</p><p>Major fortification counts as one category tougher for structural damage and grants defenders +1 Artisan bonus to checks/saves against forced entry, siege movement and collapse effects.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000110","name":"Carved Grip — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-carved-grip"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000110","name":"Carved Grip","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Carved Grip</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>+1 Artisan bonus to checks to resist Disarm or losing grip of the carved item.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000111","name":"Wolf Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-wolf-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000111","name":"Wolf Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Wolf Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>After hitting a creature, gain +5 ft Speed when moving toward that creature until end of turn.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>standard</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000112","name":"Bear Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-bear-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000112","name":"Bear Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Bear Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>While wielding/raising item, gain resistance to physical damage equal to half Core Tier, rounded up; doubles against forced-movement damage.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000113","name":"Serpent Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-serpent-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000113","name":"Serpent Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Serpent Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Weapon gains one approved flexible/reach-style property; once/round after a successful Strike, Step 5 ft without triggering reactions from that target.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000114","name":"Spirit Carving — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-spirit-carving"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000114","name":"Spirit Carving","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Spirit Carving</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Item houses a totem spirit; once/encounter activate for 1 minute to gain +1 Artisan bonus to attack or AC chosen when crafted plus a themed sense/movement benefit.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000115","name":"Totemic Ascendance — Carpentry — Warcarving","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"carpentry-specialty-3-totemic-ascendance"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000115","name":"Totemic Ascendance","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Totemic Ascendance</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Carpentry — Warcarving</p><p>Choose Wolf, Bear, Serpent or Stag each daily preparation; item gains that totem&#39;s Major-level package for the day, without consuming additional Capacity.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, haft, stock, staff, frame, grip</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): wood</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000116","name":"Stonebound — Stonemasonry — Universal","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-universal-stonebound"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000116","name":"Stonebound","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Stonebound</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Universal</p><p>+1 Hardness and +10% item/structure HP.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
