{"_id":"wmMark0000000123","name":"Grand Foundation — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-grand-foundation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000123","name":"Grand Foundation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Grand Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Structures built on this foundation gain +2 Artisan bonus against collapse, subsidence and siege movement; repairs restore 25% more HP.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000124","name":"Civic Wonder — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-civic-wonder"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000124","name":"Civic Wonder","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Civic Wonder</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Assign one Kingdom purpose at creation—Culture, Defence, Trade, Faith or Infrastructure—and grant a strong project bonus agreed for that subsystem.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>major</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>2</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>1 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000125","name":"Imperial Work — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-imperial-work"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000125","name":"Imperial Work","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Imperial Work</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Major structure reduces one related Kingdom resource cost by 25% and counts as a landmark/wonder for prestige and strategic effects.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>None</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000126","name":"World-Rooted Foundation — Stonemasonry — Megalithics","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-1-world-rooted-foundation"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000126","name":"World-Rooted Foundation","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>World-Rooted Foundation</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Megalithics</p><p>Structure cannot be moved or toppled by ordinary effects and gains resistance to siege/structural damage equal to 3 × Core Tier.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>superior</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>3</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>4</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>2 unit(s): stone</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
{"_id":"wmMark0000000127","name":"Inscribed Keystone — Stonemasonry — Runemasonry","ownership":{"default":2},"flags":{"pf2e-crafting-material-tiers":{"artisanMarkReference":"stonemason-specialty-2-inscribed-keystone"}},"pages":[{"_id":"wmMark0000000127","name":"Inscribed Keystone","type":"text","sort":100000,"title":{"show":true,"level":1},"text":{"format":1,"content":"<h2>Inscribed Keystone</h2><p><strong>Source:</strong> Stonemasonry — Runemasonry</p><p>+2 Artisan bonus to identify/repair the ward and clearly marks ownership or purpose to authorised users.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Grade</th><td>minor</td></tr><tr><th>Capacity</th><td>0</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Core Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Minimum Anchor Tier</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Anchor types</th><td>core, frame, fittings, lens</td></tr><tr><th>Item groups</th><td>weapon, armor, shield, spellFocus</td></tr><tr><th>Specialist materials</th><td>Workshop consumables only</td></tr><tr><th>Synergy tags</th><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Only one zero-Capacity Artisan Mark is allowed per new item.</p><p>Reference only. Use the Workbench or GM Item Creator to apply this Mark; those tools check the exact item and Anchor compatibility.</p>"}}]}
